  "surfaces": {
    "web-page": "Warm canvas page, white cards, one deep-orange primary action per view, pill buttons. Display type at --text-display with --tracking-display for the one page title; at most 2-3 peach feature cards per screen. Sections 80px apart (--s-9) with a hairline, not a heavy rule.",
    "artifact-report": "Inspection sheet: title, lead line, key figures, what needs the reader, then detail. Figures in white tiles on the canvas; status always as a word in a badge. No display-size type below the title; tables in a scroll container; peach feature card only for the one headline finding.",
    "dashboard": "Compact density. KPI tiles first, then charts colored accent, link blue, and ink (in that order, directly labelled), then tables. No feature cards; orange only on the active filter and the primary action. Numbers use tabular figures.",
    "slide-deck": "Spacious density, 16:9, one idea per slide. Canvas background, display type for the slide title, one peach feature card or one figure per slide, the brand orange as a small mark only. Body text at least 24px when projected.",
    "mod": "Claude Code mods draw with the host theme: a Button holds text only, so icons are characters (star, arrow) and labels are short verb-plus-object words. No colors, fonts, or radius can be set; carry the style through wording, order (most used first, one starred action), and grouping. The status line is plain text: short fields separated by a middle dot.",
    "word-document": "Body in the body face at 11pt (Segoe UI or Calibri when the web fonts are not installed), headings in the display face at weight 500, ink text on white paper. The orange accent only for heading rules and one table header row; status words in text, never color alone. Tables use hairline borders (--line), no shading except the header."
  }
